# Generated statistics data. These files are written by the scripts below in a
# deliberately compact shape — one line per series array, via the shared
# `format()` helper — so that a data refresh reviews as one changed line per
# barrio instead of one per number. Prettier expands those arrays to a value per
# line (oferta-alquiler-caba.json: ~200 lines to ~2900), which has to be reverted
# by hand and is undone again the next time the script runs.
#
#   venta-caba.json           \
#   alquiler-caba.json         >  bun run data:caba      scripts/fetch-caba-inmobiliario.ts
#   oferta-alquiler-caba.json /
#   dolar.json                    bun run data:dolar     scripts/fetch-dolar.ts
#   caba-geo.json                 bun run data:caba-geo  scripts/build-caba-geo.ts
#
# ipc-vivienda.json is hand-maintained rather than generated, but is covered by
# the same glob so that a new generated dataset dropped in this directory is
# ignored by default instead of silently reintroducing the problem.
src/content/estadisticas/data/*.json
